<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Nampak year shr, div up 14 percent.</title>
<headline>Nampak year shr, div up 14 percent.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1996-11-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended September 30</p>
<p>			(million rand unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr, attrib (cts)     104.2	 vs 91.1</p>
<p>    Div (cts)		 40	    vs 35</p>
<p>    Attrib income	   526.6	 vs 458.2</p>
<p>    Pre-tax		   798.4	 vs 736.8</p>
<p>    Tax			 254.5	 vs 266.9</p>
<p>    Interest paid	   26.7	  vs 12.6</p>
<p>    Turnover		  6,572.1     vs 5,896.7</p>
<p>Div payable January 10</p>
<p>on register November 29</p>
<p>Full name: Nampak Ltd (packaging)</p>
<p>NOTE - Analysts polled by Reuters had forecast earnings per share of 110.5 cents, with a range of 103-120, and a dividend of 39.9 cents, with a range 38-44.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
</text>
